    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "After months of strategic review, a major employer in the U.S. is letting go of roughly 17% of its workforce, a workforce reduction affecting about 3,000 people. The chief executive communicated the difficult decision to staff, framing it as an organizational transformation necessary for the company's future. While the move is positioned as building for the next chapter, it means many neighbors and colleagues are now job-hunting, and two communities will see local offices being shut down.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
        "fragments": [
          "why-1",
          "how-0",
          "result-0",
          "result-2"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The boss told workers their jobs are gone as part of a corporate restructuring aimed at accelerating AI-driven product work. Those being let go in the United States were offered a severance package, a financial cushion of 16 weeks of base pay plus additional tenure-based weeks to ease the transition. It's a painful change for individuals and the affected offices, but the company is consolidating to focus on its stated business strategy.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-1",
          "result-1",
          "result-3"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.78
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "A technology firm is making a planned workforce reduction, cutting jobs and winding down its Reno and Woodland Hills locations. This announcement means a significant portion of the team will leave, leaving people to pick up the pieces. The compensation offer of severance pay provides some employee support, but it follows an internal review where management decided this action was a necessary loss for the organization's future goals.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
